EVALUATION.md §9.2, DECISIONS 379: `[#n]` on a table warns W1912 at the segment, naming the path up to it; the same table's entry selected by key is silent, and `[#n]` on a plain list is accepted.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Tier {
  rate: Int
}

local record Cfg {
  tiers: table Tier
  xs: [Int]
}

local let cfg: Cfg = {
  tiers: { low { rate: 1 }, high { rate: 2 } }
  xs: [1, 2]
}
-- a/dev.layer.canon --
package a
layer dev

amend cfg {
  tiers[#0].rate: 3
  tiers.high.rate: 4
  xs[#1]: 5
}
-- findings.txt --
warning[W1912]  a/dev.layer.canon:5:8
  amend path tiers[#0] selects an entry by position, and the entry at a position changes when entries are added or entry files move: select it by key

0 errors, 1 warning in 1 package (…)
